@* EditGroup.razor — Salary-budget feature, Step 6

   Staff-facing customer-group detail + edit page at route
   `/Admin/Groups/{GroupId:guid}`. Reached from the row's "view details"
   button on /Admin/Groups. Role-gated to Admin / Manager / Employee via
   [Authorize(Roles=...)] as defense-in-depth. The page-level gate is the
   first cut; the mutating command handlers enforce stricter rules
   server-side (RenameCustomerGroup / UpdateCustomerGroupSalary /
   ActivateCustomerGroup / DeactivateCustomerGroup all require Manager or
   Admin).

   PURPOSE:
     This page is the admin/manager's view of a single customer group.
     It exists so they can:
       1. See the group's full state (Name, Salary, Status, audit dates,
          active user count).
       2. Rename the group (RenameCustomerGroupCommand).
       3. Change the salary amount (UpdateCustomerGroupSalaryCommand —
          note: currency cannot be changed; see the warning card).
       4. Activate or Deactivate the group
          (ActivateCustomerGroupCommand / DeactivateCustomerGroupCommand).
       5. Bulk-apply default purchase limits to every product that
          doesn't already have a limit for this group
          (BulkApplyDefaultsForGroupCommand — closes the "reactivation
          gap" documented since Step 5: when a group is deactivated and
          new products are added during the inactive period, those new
          products have NO limit row for the group; this button fills
          them in with the default limit of 1).

   STYLE PARITY WITH SETTINGS / PRODUCTDETAIL:
     Mirrors the Settings.razor + ProductDetail.razor detail-page
     pattern:
       - Same .create-grid layout (2fr form + 1fr help/info panel).
       - Same .form-section vertical-stack of fields.
       - Same .form-actions row at the bottom.
       - Same .profile-grid pattern (label/value pairs) for the read-only
         summary at the top.
       - Same .section-title pattern for card headings.

   ROLE-SCOPE FOR ACTIONS:
     - View + Navigate: Admin / Manager / Employee (page-level gate).
     - Edit (Rename / Salary): Manager + Admin only. Employees see the
       summary card only (form is hidden).
     - Activate/Deactivate: Manager + Admin only.
     - Bulk Apply Defaults: Manager + Admin only, AND group must be
       active. Closes the "reactivation gap" (see command XML doc).

   LOADING / ERROR / NOT-FOUND STATES:
     The page shows distinct states for: loading spinner, load-failed
     error, not-found (the {GroupId} doesn't exist in the DB), and the
     normal loaded state. The not-found case is detected server-side
     (GetCustomerGroupByIdQueryHandler returns Failure with "not found"
     if the group doesn't exist) and we surface it as a friendly
     "group not found" card with a back-to-list button.

   LOCALIZATION:
     All user-visible strings via IStringLocalizer<EditGroup> (Loc).
     Keys defined in EditGroup.en-US.resx + EditGroup.fa-IR.resx. *@

@page "/Admin/Groups/{GroupId:guid}"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager,Employee")]
@using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations
@using System.Globalization
@using System.Text
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Commands.ActivateCustomerGroup
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Commands.BulkApplyDefaultsForGroup
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Commands.DeactivateCustomerGroup
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Commands.RenameCustomerGroup
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Commands.UpdateCustomerGroupSalary
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Queries.GetCustomerGroupById
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.WebUI.Components.Dialogs.DeactivateGroupDialog
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<EditGroup> Loc
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject ErrorDisplayService ErrorDisplay
@inject Radzen.DialogService DialogService
@inject IJSRuntime JS
@inject Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILogger<EditGroup> Logger

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            .edit-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
                gap: 2rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .edit-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1.25rem;
                }
            }

            .form-section {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 1.25rem;
            }

            .salary-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                align-items: flex-end;
            }

                .salary-row .salary-amount {
                    flex: 1 1 auto;
                }

                .salary-row .salary-currency {
                    flex: 0 0 180px;
                }

            .form-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                margin-top: 1rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            .form-error {
                margin-bottom: 1rem;
            }

            /* Summary card — read-only label/value pairs in a 2-col grid.
                                                   Mirrors Settings.razor's .profile-grid pattern. */
            .profile-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(120px, auto) 1fr;
                gap: 0.625rem 1.25rem;
                align-items: baseline;
            }

            .profile-label {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                font-weight: 500;
            }

            .profile-value {
                font-size: 0.9375rem;
            }

            .profile-value-mono {
                font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace;
                direction: ltr;
                display: inline-block;
            }

            /* Section title — small heading inside a card with a leading icon.
                                                   Mirrors Settings.razor's .section-title pattern. */
            .section-title {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
            }

            .help-panel {
                position: sticky;
                top: 1rem;
            }

                .help-panel ul {
                    margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;
                    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    line-height: 1.7;
                }

                .help-panel li {
                    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
                }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .help-panel {
                    position: static;
                }
            }

            /* RTL fallback for RadzenNumeric — the inner input is forced
                                                   LTR so the caret + digit grouping reads correctly in both
                                                   LTR and RTL layouts. */
            .salary-row .rz-numeric .rz-textbox {
                direction: ltr;
                text-align: left;
            }

            /* Currency-read-only pill — shown next to the salary amount
                                                   field to communicate "you can edit the amount, but the
                                                   currency is locked". Mirrors the .salary-currency span
                                                   pattern used on the ManageGroups list page. */
            .currency-locked-pill {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;
                border-radius: 999px;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color, #f3f4f6);
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color);
                color: var(--rz-text-color);
                font-size: 0.8125rem;
                font-weight: 500;
                direction: ltr;
                white-space: nowrap;
            }

                .currency-locked-pill .currency-locked-icon {
                    color: var(--rz-text-tertiary-color, #9ca3af);
                    font-size: 0.95rem;
                }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Breadcrumb + back button ── *@
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToManageGroups"]"
                      Icon="arrow_back"
                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Groups", forceLoad: false))" />
    </RadzenStack>

    @* ── Loading state ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["Loading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Error state — load failure (DB error, etc.) ── *@
    else if (_loadError is not null && _group is null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Not-found state — the {GroupId} doesn't exist ──
       The handler returns "Customer group '...' was not found." for both
       genuinely-missing groups AND not-allowed-to-see (defense-in-depth
       — same pattern as UserDetail.razor). We surface a friendly card. *@
    else if (_group is null)
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 2.5rem; text-align: center;">
            <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center" Gap="1rem">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="search_off" Style="font-size: 3rem; color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["NotFoundTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["NotFoundBody"]"
                            TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); max-width: 480px; margin: 0;" />
                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToManageGroups"]"
                              Icon="arrow_back"
                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                              Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Groups", forceLoad: false))" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Loaded state ── *@
    else
    {
        @* ── Page header — name + status badge ──
           The header uses flex-wrap (via the inline style) so on narrow
           screens the status badge drops below the name instead of
           overflowing horizontally. Same pattern as AdminUsers's
           admin-header (which uses flex-wrap: wrap on the container). *@
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem" Style="flex-wrap: wrap;">
            <RadzenIcon Icon="diversity_3" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
            <RadzenText Text="@_group.Name" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
            <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(_group.IsActive)"
                         BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(_group.IsActive)"
                         IsPill="true" />
        </RadzenStack>

        <div class="edit-grid">
            @* LEFT — summary + edit form *@
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
                @* ── Summary card — read-only label/value pairs ──
                   Always shown (to all roles). The admin/manager-only edit
                   form is rendered separately below. Employees see ONLY
                   this card (no edit form). *@
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.5rem;">
                    <div class="section-title">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="info" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                        <span>@Loc["SummaryCardTitle"]</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="profile-grid">
                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColName"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">@_group.Name</div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColSalary"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value profile-value-mono">
                            @FormatSalaryAmount(_group.Salary.Amount)
                            <span style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); font-size: 0.8125rem; margin-inline-start: 0.25rem;">@_group.Salary.Currency</span>
                        </div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColStatus"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">
                            <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(_group.IsActive)"
                                         BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(_group.IsActive)"
                                         IsPill="true" />
                        </div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColActiveUsers"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">
                            @if (_group.ActiveUserCount == 0)
                            {
                                <span style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">@Loc["NoActiveUsers"]</span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <span>@FormatInt(_group.ActiveUserCount)</span>
                            }
                        </div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColCreatedAt"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value profile-value-mono">@FormatDate(_group.CreatedAtUtc)</div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColUpdatedAt"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value profile-value-mono">@FormatDate(_group.UpdatedAtUtc)</div>
                    </div>
                </RadzenCard>

                @* ── Edit form — Manager + Admin only ──
                   Employees see the summary card only. The form is gated
                   both client-side (Visible) AND server-side (each command
                   requires Manager or Admin role). *@
                @if (_isAdmin || _isManagerOnly)
                {
                    <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.5rem;">
                        <EditForm Model="@_model"
                                  OnValidSubmit="@HandleSubmitAsync"
                                  OnInvalidSubmit="@HandleInvalidSubmit"
                                  FormName="editGroup">
                            <DataAnnotationsValidator />

                            @* Server-side error banner (e.g. name collision). *@
                            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_submitError))
                            {
                                <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                                             Text="@_submitError"
                                             AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                             Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                             ShowIcon="true"
                                             Class="form-error" />
                            }

                            <div class="form-section">
                                @* ── Name (editable) ── *@
                                <div>
                                    <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldName"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                        <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_model.Name"
                                                       Placeholder="@Loc["FieldNamePlaceholder"]"
                                                       TValue="string"
                                                       Style="width: 100%;" />
                                    </RadzenFormField>
                                </div>

                                @* ── Salary Amount (editable) + Currency (locked) ──
                                   The amount is editable via UpdateCustomerGroupSalaryCommand.
                                   The currency is LOCKED — changing currency would
                                   invalidate already-purchased products priced in the
                                   old currency. To use a different currency, the admin
                                   must deactivate this group and create a new one
                                   (see help panel). The currency is shown as a
                                   read-only pill to communicate this visually.

                                   AMOUNT TEXTBOX:
                                     We use a RadzenTextBox bound to a STRING field
                                     (_salaryAmountText), NOT a RadzenNumeric bound
                                     to a decimal. Three reasons:
                                       1. IRR amounts are whole Rial — we never want
                                          to show 2 decimal digits. RadzenNumeric
                                          with TValue=decimal defaults to 2 decimals
                                          and there's no clean way to make Decimals
                                          conditional on the currency at runtime.
                                       2. We need thousands separators (N0 format).
                                          RadzenNumeric.Format="N0" DOES add them,
                                          BUT only when the input is NOT focused —
                                          and even then .NET's NativeDigits is
                                          informational-only (see CultureFormat.cs
                                          header comment), so the digits come out
                                          ASCII in fa-IR mode.
                                       3. We need Persian digits (۰-۹) when the UI
                                          culture is fa-IR. The only reliable way
                                          to get Persian digits out of .NET is the
                                          manual swap in CultureFormat.ToCultureDigits.
                                          That swap has to happen on a STRING we
                                          control — not inside RadzenNumeric.
                                     So: bind a string, format on blur, parse on
                                     focus. The user edits the raw invariant number
                                     while the input is focused (easy typing, no
                                     separators to fight with), and sees the
                                     formatted (thousand-separated, Persian-digit)
                                     form when not editing. *@
                                <div>
                                    <RadzenText Text="@Loc["FieldSalary"]"
                                                TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                                Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;" />

                                    <div class="salary-row">
                                        <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldAmount"]" Class="salary-amount" Style="width: 100%;">
                                            <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_salaryAmountText"
                                                           TValue="string"
                                                           Style="width: 100%; direction: ltr; text-align: left;"
                                                           Placeholder="@Loc["FieldAmountPlaceholder"]"
                                                           @onfocus="OnSalaryAmountFocus"
                                                           @onblur="OnSalaryAmountBlur" />
                                        </RadzenFormField>

                                        <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldCurrency"]" Class="salary-currency" Style="width: 100%;">
                                            <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; height: 100%; padding-block: 0.4rem;">
                                                <span class="currency-locked-pill" title="@Loc["CurrencyLockedTitle"]">
                                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="lock" Class="currency-locked-icon" />
                                                    @_model.SalaryCurrency
                                                </span>
                                            </div>
                                        </RadzenFormField>
                                    </div>

                                    <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                                Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.25rem;">
                                        @Loc["SalaryHint"]
                                    </RadzenText>
                                </div>

                                @* ── Form actions ──
                                   Save (primary, submit) + Cancel (secondary outlined,
                                   navigates back to /Admin/Groups) + Activate/Deactivate
                                   toggle (depends on current status). *@
                                <div class="form-actions">
                                    @if (_group.IsActive)
                                    {
                                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["DeactivateButton"]"
                                                      Icon="block"
                                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                      Disabled="@_isSubmitting"
                                                      Click="@HandleDeactivateAsync" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActivateButton"]"
                                                      Icon="check_circle"
                                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Success"
                                                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                      Disabled="@_isSubmitting"
                                                      Click="@HandleActivateAsync" />
                                    }

                                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                                  Icon="close"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                  Disabled="@_isSubmitting"
                                                  Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Groups", forceLoad: false))" />

                                    <RadzenButton ButtonType="ButtonType.Submit"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                                  Disabled="@_isSubmitting">
                                        @* ChildContent (this @if block) takes precedence over
                                           the Text= and Icon= parameters on RadzenButton —
                                           once any child content exists, Radzen stops rendering
                                           Text/Icon. So we render the icon + text EXPLICITLY
                                           here, swapping to a spinner while submitting. This
                                           is the only way to keep the button text visible
                                           AND show an inline spinner during submit. *@
                                        @if (_isSubmitting)
                                        {
                                            <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false"
                                                                       Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate"
                                                                       Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Small"
                                                                       Style="margin-inline-end: 0.5rem;" />
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            <RadzenIcon Icon="save" Style="margin-inline-end: 0.5rem;" />
                                        }
                                        <span>@Loc["SaveButton"]</span>
                                    </RadzenButton>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </EditForm>
                    </RadzenCard>

                    @* ── Bulk Apply Defaults card — Manager + Admin only, group must be active ──
                       Closes the "reactivation gap" documented since Step 5:
                       when a group is deactivated and new products are added
                       during the inactive period, those new products do NOT
                       get default purchase-limit rows for the inactive group
                       (CreateProduct Phase-1 auto-default loop only iterates
                       ACTIVE groups, by design). On reactivation, this button
                       fills that gap by bulk-applying the default limit (1)
                       to every product missing a limit row for this group.

                       The button is rendered only when:
                         - User is Admin or Manager (server enforces too via
                           [RequireRoles] on the command); AND
                         - Group is active (the handler also rejects inactive
                           groups with a friendly error — the UI hides the
                           button preemptively to avoid a dead-end click).

                       The card is visually distinct (Warning tone + auto_fix_high
                       icon) to signal that this is a bulk operation across
                       the entire catalog, not a single-row mutation. The
                       JS.confirm() dialog explains the semantics before the
                       user commits. *@
                    @if (_group.IsActive)
                    {
                        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.5rem; border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--rz-warning-color, #f59e0b);">
                            <div class="section-title">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="auto_fix_high" Style="color: var(--rz-warning-color, #f59e0b);" />
                                <span>@Loc["BulkDefaultsCardTitle"]</span>
                            </div>

                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-bottom: 1rem; line-height: 1.6;">
                                @Loc["BulkDefaultsDescription"]
                            </RadzenText>

                            <div class="form-actions">
                                <RadzenButton ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Warning"
                                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                              Disabled="@(_isSubmitting || _isBulkApplyingDefaults)"
                                              Click="@HandleBulkApplyDefaultsAsync">
                                    @* ChildContent (this @if block) takes precedence over
                                       Text= and Icon= on RadzenButton — render the icon +
                                       text EXPLICITLY here so the label stays visible.
                                       See the SaveButton above for the full explanation. *@
                                    @if (_isBulkApplyingDefaults)
                                    {
                                        <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false"
                                                                   Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate"
                                                                   Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Small"
                                                                   Style="margin-inline-end: 0.5rem;" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="auto_fix_high" Style="margin-inline-end: 0.5rem;" />
                                    }
                                    <span>@Loc["BulkApplyDefaultsButton"]</span>
                                </RadzenButton>
                            </div>
                        </RadzenCard>
                    }
                }
            </RadzenStack>

            @* RIGHT — help / info panel. Explains:
                 - What "rename" does (does NOT affect existing references).
                 - What "salary update" does (takes effect immediately for
                   new purchases; doesn't retroactively change consumed
                   amount for this month — could make remaining budget
                   negative).
                 - Why currency is locked (would invalidate already-
                   purchased products priced in the old currency).
                 - What "deactivate" does (blocks new purchases by users
                   in this group; submitted sales are kept). *@
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Outlined" Class="help-panel" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <div class="section-title">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="help_outline" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                        <span>@Loc["HelpCardTitle"]</span>
                    </div>
                    <ul>
                        <li>@Loc["HelpLine_Rename"]</li>
                        <li>@Loc["HelpLine_SalaryImmediate"]</li>
                        <li>@Loc["HelpLine_SalaryNegative"]</li>
                        <li>@Loc["HelpLine_CurrencyLocked"]</li>
                        <li>@Loc["HelpLine_Deactivate"]</li>
                    </ul>
                </RadzenCard>
            </RadzenStack>
        </div>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── Route parameter ───────────────────────────────────────────────

    [Parameter]
    public Guid GroupId { get; set; }

    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private CustomerGroupDto? _group;

    private bool _isLoading = true;
    private string? _loadError;
    private bool _isSubmitting;
    private string? _submitError;

    /// <summary>
    /// Separate spinner flag for the "Bulk Apply Defaults" button. Kept
    /// distinct from <see cref="_isSubmitting"/> purely so the bulk
    /// button can render its OWN inline spinner (the form-action buttons
    /// don't show a spinner, they just go disabled). During a bulk
    /// operation, BOTH flags are set true — <see cref="_isSubmitting"/>
    /// disables the form-action buttons (Save/Activate/Deactivate/Cancel),
    /// and <see cref="_isBulkApplyingDefaults"/> shows the inline spinner
    /// in the bulk button itself. See <see cref="HandleBulkApplyDefaultsAsync"/>.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isBulkApplyingDefaults;

    /// <summary>
    /// The text shown in the Salary Amount textbox. Bound to a STRING (not a
    /// decimal) so we can format it ourselves: thousands separators + Persian
    /// digits (in fa-IR mode) + 0 decimal places when the currency is IRR.
    /// See the comment block above the textbox in the markup for the full
    /// rationale of why RadzenNumeric + decimal wasn't suitable.
    ///
    /// SYNC CONTRACT:
    ///   - Set on load (LoadGroupAsync) to the formatted display value.
    ///   - On focus: parsed to a decimal, then re-stored as the raw invariant
    ///     string (e.g. "1234567") so the user can edit easily without
    ///     fighting separators.
    ///   - On blur: parsed to a decimal, then re-stored as the formatted
    ///     display value (e.g. "1,234,567" in en-US, "۱٬۲۳۴٬۵۶۷" in fa-IR),
    ///     AND propagated to _model.SalaryAmount for form submission.
    ///   - On submit (HandleSubmitAsync): re-parsed from text to decimal
    ///     defensively, in case the user clicked Save while the textbox was
    ///     still focused (so onblur hadn't fired yet — RadzenButton clicks
    ///     fire AFTER blur, but a JS-initiated submit or Enter-key submit
    ///     could race).
    /// </summary>
    private string _salaryAmountText = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The form model. Bound via EditForm + DataAnnotationsValidator —
    /// the [Required] + [StringLength] + [Range] attributes below
    /// provide the FIRST wave of validation (fires in OnValidSubmit /
    /// OnInvalidSubmit). The respective command validators provide the
    /// SECOND wave server-side via Wolverine's pipeline.
    /// </summary>
    private sealed class EditGroupForm
    {
        [Required(ErrorMessage = "ValidationError_NameRequired")]
        [StringLength(100, ErrorMessage = "ValidationError_NameLength")]
        public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "ValidationError_AmountRequired")]
        [Range(0, double.MaxValue, ErrorMessage = "ValidationError_AmountRange")]
        public decimal SalaryAmount { get; set; }

        /// <summary>
        /// Currency is read-only — bound from the loaded group, never
        /// edited. Shown as a locked pill in the form. The
        /// UpdateCustomerGroupSalaryCommand only accepts the amount;
        /// currency is preserved on the existing aggregate.
        /// </summary>
        public string SalaryCurrency { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    }

    private readonly EditGroupForm _model = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the current user is in the Admin role. Computed via
    /// AuthenticationStateProvider in OnInitializedAsync — NOT via
    /// ICurrentUserService.IsInRole (which returns false for everyone
    /// in interactive Blazor Server mode because HttpContext is null
    /// over the SignalR circuit). Same pattern as AdminUsers.razor.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isAdmin;

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the current user is in the Manager role (and NOT also in
    /// the Admin role). Used to gate the edit form + Activate/Deactivate
    /// buttons (Manager + Admin can act).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isManagerOnly;

    // ── Lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Resolve the current user's Admin/Manager roles via the Blazor auth
        // state (NOT ICurrentUserService — see field doc on _isAdmin).
        try
        {
            var authState = await AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
            var user = authState.User;

            if (user?.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true)
            {
                _isAdmin = user.IsInRole(Roles.Admin);
                _isManagerOnly = !_isAdmin && user.IsInRole(Roles.Manager);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            // Non-fatal — _isAdmin stays false (edit form hidden — safer
            // fallback if role resolution fails).
        }

        await LoadGroupAsync();
    }

    // ── Data loading ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadGroupAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;
        _loadError = null;
        _submitError = null;

        try
        {
            var query = new GetCustomerGroupByIdQuery { GroupId = GroupId };
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<CustomerGroupDto>>(query);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                _group = result.Value;

                // Pre-fill the form model with the loaded group's values.
                // If the user navigates away without saving, the form is
                // discarded along with the component.
                _model.Name = _group.Name;
                _model.SalaryAmount = _group.Salary.Amount;
                _model.SalaryCurrency = _group.Salary.Currency;

                // Initialize the textbox's display text with the formatted
                // value (thousand-separated, Persian digits in fa-IR, 0
                // decimals when currency is IRR). The user will see the
                // formatted value on first render; clicking into the field
                // switches to the raw number for editing (see
                // OnSalaryAmountFocus).
                _salaryAmountText = FormatSalaryForDisplay(_model.SalaryAmount);
            }
            else
            {
                // The handler returns "Customer group '...' was not found."
                // for both genuinely-missing groups AND not-allowed-to-see.
                // We treat this as "not found" — the markup renders the
                // NotFound card when _group is null.
                _loadError = result.Error;
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            _loadError = Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Submit handlers ───────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Called when EditForm validation passes. Dispatches BOTH the
    /// RenameCustomerGroupCommand (if Name changed) AND the
    /// UpdateCustomerGroupSalaryCommand (if SalaryAmount changed).
    /// Both run in their own Wolverine transaction — if either fails,
    /// the other is NOT rolled back (they're independent mutations on
    /// the same aggregate; the user can fix the failing one and retry).
    ///
    /// DESIGN CHOICE: We could have a single "UpdateCustomerGroupCommand"
    /// that does both, but the existing commands are atomic per-field
    /// (Rename and UpdateSalary), and they each have their own validation
    /// + audit log entry. Combining them would lose that granularity.
    /// The two-command approach is cleaner.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleSubmitAsync()
    {
        if (_group is null) return;

        _submitError = null;
        _isSubmitting = true;

        try
        {
            _model.Name = _model.Name.Trim();

            // Defensive re-parse of the salary textbox. Normally OnBlur
            // fires before the submit button's click handler does, but a
            // JS-initiated submit or Enter-key submit could race. Parsing
            // here too guarantees _model.SalaryAmount reflects whatever
            // the user typed, even if OnBlur hasn't run yet.
            //
            // If parsing fails (user typed garbage), we leave _model.SalaryAmount
            // alone — DataAnnotationsValidator's [Range] attribute will catch
            // an out-of-range value, and the OnInvalidSubmit handler will
            // surface the validation error. We DON'T set SalaryAmount to 0
            // because that would mask the real "invalid input" issue with
            // a misleading "amount changed to 0" success.
            if (TryParseAmount(_salaryAmountText, out var parsedAmount))
            {
                _model.SalaryAmount = parsedAmount;
            }

            var nameChanged = !string.Equals(_model.Name, _group.Name, StringComparison.Ordinal);
            var amountChanged = _model.SalaryAmount != _group.Salary.Amount;

            if (!nameChanged && !amountChanged)
            {
                // No-op — nothing to save. Show a friendly toast and
                // navigate back to the list.
                await Toast.Info(Loc["NoChanges"], summary: Loc["NoChangesTitle"]);
                Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Groups", forceLoad: false);
                return;
            }

            // 1. Rename if changed.
            if (nameChanged)
            {
                var renameResult = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                    new RenameCustomerGroupCommand(_group.Id, _model.Name));

                if (!renameResult.IsSuccess)
                {
                    _submitError = renameResult.Error ?? Loc["Error_Generic"];
                    return;
                }
            }

            // 2. Update salary amount if changed.
            if (amountChanged)
            {
                var salaryResult = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                    new UpdateCustomerGroupSalaryCommand(_group.Id, _model.SalaryAmount));

                if (!salaryResult.IsSuccess)
                {
                    _submitError = salaryResult.Error ?? Loc["Error_Generic"];
                    return;
                }
            }

            await Toast.Success(Loc["SuccessTitle"], summary: Loc["SuccessSummary"]);
            Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Groups", forceLoad: false);
        }
        catch
        {
            _submitError = Loc["Error_Generic"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isSubmitting = false;
        }
    }

    private Task HandleInvalidSubmit()
    {
        _submitError = null;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    // ── Activate / Deactivate ───────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task HandleDeactivateAsync()
    {
        if (_group is null) return;
        if (_isSubmitting) return;

        // Custom in-app confirmation dialog (DeactivateGroupDialog) with a
        // 3-second countdown — same pattern as DeactivateUserDialog and the
        // ManageGroups page. Replaces the old window.confirm() call.
        object? confirmed;
        try
        {
            confirmed = await DialogService.OpenAsync<DeactivateGroupDialog>(
                Loc["DeactivateDialogTitle"],
                new Dictionary<string, object?>
                {
                    { "GroupName", _group.Name }
                },
                new Radzen.DialogOptions
                {
                    Width = "420px",
                    Resizable = false,
                    Draggable = true,
                    CloseDialogOnOverlayClick = false,
                    ShowClose = true,
                });
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            // Brutal Code Review v3 finding #24, part 2: replaced
            // `System.Diagnostics.Debug.WriteLine(...)` with
            // `Logger.LogWarning(...)`. Debug.WriteLine is stripped in
            // Release builds (so production lost the diagnostic), doesn't
            // go through the logging pipeline (so it isn't filtered /
            // structured / centralized), and clutters the VS Immediate
            // Window. LogWarning flows through ILogger → the configured
            // sinks (Console / Debug / OpenTelemetry) and survives into
            // production. Severity = Warning (not Error) because the user
            // already sees a friendly toast via Toast.UnexpectedError below
            // — this isn't a fatal, request-failing exception, it's an
            // unexpected UI-dialog-open failure that warrants operator
            // attention but doesn't crash the circuit. The exception
            // instance is passed as a structured argument (named
            // "Exception" — passes the ForbiddenLoggingAnalyzer's
            // banned-token check: "Exception" is not in the banned-token
            // list [DIAG Login, PasswordLength, EmailConfirmed,
            // LockoutEnd, AccessFailedCount, Password=, Password:]).
            Logger.LogWarning("HandleDeactivateAsync: dialog open failed: {Exception}", ex);
            await Toast.UnexpectedError(UnexpectedErrorCodes.EditGroup_DialogOpen, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        if (confirmed is not true) return;

        _isSubmitting = true;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new DeactivateCustomerGroupCommand(_group.Id));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["DeactivateSuccess"], _group.Name),
                    summary: Loc["DeactivateSuccessTitle"]);
                await LoadGroupAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(ErrorDisplay.Localize(result.Error) ?? Loc["Error_Generic"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.UnexpectedError(UnexpectedErrorCodes.EditGroup_RenameFailure, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isSubmitting = false;
        }
    }

    private async Task HandleActivateAsync()
    {
        if (_group is null) return;
        if (_isSubmitting) return;

        // No confirmation for activation — it's a non-destructive restore.
        _isSubmitting = true;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new ActivateCustomerGroupCommand(_group.Id));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActivateSuccess"], _group.Name),
                    summary: Loc["ActivateSuccessTitle"]);
                await LoadGroupAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(ErrorDisplay.Localize(result.Error) ?? Loc["Error_Generic"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.UnexpectedError(UnexpectedErrorCodes.EditGroup_SalaryUpdateFailure, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isSubmitting = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Bulk Apply Defaults ──────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Dispatches <see cref="BulkApplyDefaultsForGroupCommand"/> for the
    /// current group. The command scans every product in the catalog and
    /// inserts a default purchase-limit row (= 1) wherever one is missing
    /// for this group — closing the "reactivation gap" where new products
    /// created during the group's inactive period have no limit row.
    ///
    /// FLOW:
    ///   1. JS.confirm() dialog explaining what's about to happen (the
    ///      operation is idempotent but bulk — confirmation prevents
    ///      accidental clicks).
    ///   2. Set BOTH <see cref="_isSubmitting"/> (disables form-action
    ///      buttons to prevent concurrent mutations) AND
    ///      <see cref="_isBulkApplyingDefaults"/> (shows the inline
    ///      spinner on the bulk button itself).
    ///   3. Dispatch command. The handler does its own batching + per-
    ///      batch SaveChanges; this UI thread just awaits the final result.
    ///   4. On success, show a toast with the breakdown: how many products
    ///      received the default, how many already had limits, total
    ///      scanned, and the applied limit value.
    ///   5. On "no updates needed" (every product already had a limit),
    ///      show an Info toast instead of Success — the user should know
    ///      nothing changed.
    ///   6. On failure, show the server's error message via Error toast.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleBulkApplyDefaultsAsync()
    {
        if (_group is null) return;
        if (_isSubmitting || _isBulkApplyingDefaults) return;

        var confirmed = await JS.InvokeAsync<bool>("confirm",
            string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ConfirmBulkApplyDefaults"], _group.Name));

        if (!confirmed) return;

        // Set BOTH flags: _isSubmitting disables the form-action buttons
        // (Save / Activate / Deactivate / Cancel) to prevent concurrent
        // mutations; _isBulkApplyingDefaults shows the inline spinner on
        // the bulk button itself.
        _isSubmitting = true;
        _isBulkApplyingDefaults = true;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<BulkApplyDefaultsResult>>(
                new BulkApplyDefaultsForGroupCommand(_group.Id));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                var r = result.Value;

                if (r.ProductsUpdated == 0)
                {
                    // Idempotent no-op — every product already had a limit.
                    // Use Info tone (not Success) to communicate "nothing changed".
                    await Toast.Info(
                        string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
                            Loc["BulkApplyDefaultsNoUpdates"], r.TotalProductsScanned),
                        summary: Loc["BulkApplyDefaultsTitle"]);
                }
                else
                {
                    await Toast.Success(
                        string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
                            Loc["BulkApplyDefaultsSuccess"],
                            r.ProductsUpdated, r.TotalProductsScanned,
                            r.ProductsSkipped, r.AppliedLimit),
                        summary: Loc["BulkApplyDefaultsTitle"]);
                }
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(ErrorDisplay.Localize(result.Error) ?? Loc["Error_Generic"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.UnexpectedError(UnexpectedErrorCodes.EditGroup_LimitModeSaveFailure, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBulkApplyingDefaults = false;
            _isSubmitting = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Display helpers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private string GetStatusLabel(bool isActive)
        => isActive ? Loc["StatusActive"] : Loc["StatusInactive"];

    private BadgeStyle GetStatusBadgeStyle(bool isActive)
        => isActive ? BadgeStyle.Success : BadgeStyle.Danger;

    private string FormatSalaryAmount(decimal amount)
        => CultureFormat.FormatNumber(amount);

    private string FormatInt(int value)
        => CultureFormat.FormatDigits(value);

    // ── Salary amount textbox helpers ────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a decimal salary amount for DISPLAY in the textbox (i.e.
    /// when the input is NOT focused). Returns a string with:
    ///   - Persian digits (۰-۹) when the UI culture is fa-IR, ASCII (0-9)
    ///     otherwise — via <see cref="CultureFormat.ToCultureDigits"/>.
    ///   - Thousands separators ("," in en-US, "٬" in fa-IR — also handled
    ///     by ToCultureDigits since the .NET N0 format produces commas
    ///     and ToCultureDigits swaps them).
    ///   - 0 decimal places when the currency is IRR (whole-Rial — Iran's
    ///     currency has no fractional unit in practice for salary values).
    ///     2 decimal places for other currencies (USD, EUR, etc.).
    /// </summary>
    private string FormatSalaryForDisplay(decimal amount)
    {
        var isIrr = string.Equals(_model.SalaryCurrency, "IRR",
            StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        // N0 = no decimals, with thousands separators.
        // N2 = 2 decimal places, with thousands separators.
        // InvariantCulture produces ASCII digits + comma separators; we then
        // run ToCultureDigits to swap them for Persian digits + ٬ separator
        // when the UI culture is fa-IR.
        var fmt = isIrr ? "N0" : "N2";
        return CultureFormat.ToCultureDigits(
            amount.ToString(fmt, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Parses a string the user typed into the salary amount textbox into
    /// a decimal. Accepts:
    ///   - ASCII digits "0"-"9"
    ///   - Persian digits "۰"-"۹" (converted to ASCII before parsing)
    ///   - Thousands separators "," and "٬" (ignored)
    ///   - Decimal separator "." (ASCII) or "٫" (Persian) — both converted
    ///     to "." for the InvariantCulture parser
    ///   - Leading/trailing whitespace (trimmed)
    /// Returns false on any parse failure (caller decides what to do —
    /// usually leaves _model.SalaryAmount alone and lets validation catch
    /// the bad input).
    /// </summary>
    private static bool TryParseAmount(string? input, out decimal amount)
    {
        amount = 0m;
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(input)) return false;

        // Normalize: strip separators, convert Persian digits/decimal-point
        // to ASCII equivalents, then parse with InvariantCulture.
        var sb = new StringBuilder(input.Length);
        foreach (var c in input.Trim())
        {
            if (c == ',' || c == '٬') continue;       // thousands separator
            if (c == '٫') sb.Append('.');              // Persian decimal point
            else if (c >= '۰' && c <= '۹')
                sb.Append((char)('0' + (c - '۰')));    // Persian digit → ASCII
            else sb.Append(c);
        }

        return decimal.TryParse(sb.ToString(),
            NumberStyles.Number, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out amount);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Fired when the salary amount textbox gains focus. Switches the
    /// displayed text from the formatted (thousand-separated, Persian-digit)
    /// form to the raw invariant number so the user can edit easily
    /// without fighting separators. If the current text doesn't parse
    /// (e.g. user typed garbage that we couldn't format on a previous
    /// blur), we leave the text alone so the user can see what they typed.
    /// </summary>
    private void OnSalaryAmountFocus()
    {
        if (TryParseAmount(_salaryAmountText, out var amount))
        {
            // InvariantCulture produces ASCII digits + "." decimal separator
            // — the safest form for free-text editing. No thousands separators
            // (they'd just get in the way while typing).
            _salaryAmountText = amount.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
        }
        // else: leave the text alone so the user can fix whatever they typed.
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Fired when the salary amount textbox loses focus. Parses the current
    /// text to a decimal, propagates it to <see cref="EditGroupForm.SalaryAmount"/>
    /// (so the form's [Range] validation can fire on the real value), and
    /// re-formats the displayed text with thousand separators + Persian
    /// digits (in fa-IR) + 0 decimals (in IRR). If parsing fails, we leave
    /// both the text and _model.SalaryAmount alone — DataAnnotationsValidator
    /// will surface a validation error via the [Required] + [Range] attrs.
    /// </summary>
    private void OnSalaryAmountBlur()
    {
        if (TryParseAmount(_salaryAmountText, out var amount))
        {
            _model.SalaryAmount = amount;
            _salaryAmountText = FormatSalaryForDisplay(amount);
        }
        // else: leave text + SalaryAmount alone — validation will fire on submit.
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a UTC DateTime as a localized date-time string in Tehran
    /// time, culture-aware. Delegates to
    /// <see cref="CultureFormat.FormatTehranDateTime(DateTime)"/>, which
    /// produces Persian digits + Jalali date in fa-IR mode and ASCII
    /// digits + Gregorian date in en-US mode. The previous implementation
    /// used <c>local.ToString("g", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)</c>, which
    /// produced ASCII digits in fa-IR mode and a Gregorian year (because
    /// .NET's fa-IR culture's default calendar is Gregorian, not Jalali).
    /// </summary>
    private string FormatDate(DateTime utc)
        => CultureFormat.FormatTehranDateTime(utc);
}